{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "63dda07f-7c50-42e2-9eb7-81045d5cc646",
    "name": "WU System — Seed Majors",
    "description": "Standalone collection to create the majors list Leng provided, via the existing Major CRUD endpoint (POST /api/v1/majors). Not part of the wu_system codebase — just a Postman collection for manual/API-side data entry.\n\nAuth: this app uses Laravel Breeze session auth (not token-based), so requests need a valid session cookie + the matching X-XSRF-TOKEN header. Run '1. Get CSRF Cookie' then '2. Login' once (per Postman session) before running the Seed Majors folder — Postman's cookie jar carries the session forward automatically for the rest of the collection.\n\nBefore running:\n- Set 'base_url' to your local/dev URL (e.g. http://localhost:8000).\n- Set 'email' / 'password' to a real user with the 'major.create' permission (an Admin account works).\n- Set 'faculty_id' to a real, existing faculty ID — every major here needs one; if these 17 majors span more than one faculty, edit faculty_id per request instead of using the shared variable.\n- Fill in each request's 'name_kh' — left as a placeholder since the Khmer names weren't provided.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8000"
    },
    {
      "key": "email",
      "value": "admin@system.me"
    },
    {
      "key": "password",
      "value": "CHANGE_ME"
    },
    {
      "key": "faculty_id",
      "value": "1"
    }
  ],
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Attach the XSRF-TOKEN cookie (set by Laravel's VerifyCsrfToken middleware",
          "// on any 'web' route response) as the X-XSRF-TOKEN header, the same way",
          "// Laravel's own front-end (axios) does it for stateful/session requests.",
          "const base = pm.collectionVariables.get('base_url');",
          "const jar = pm.cookies.jar();",
          "if (base) {",
          "    jar.get(base, 'XSRF-TOKEN', (err, token) => {",
          "        if (!err && token) {",
          "            pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'X-XSRF-TOKEN', value: decodeURIComponent(token) });",
          "        }",
          "    });",
          "}",
          ""
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Get CSRF Cookie",
          "id": "f6af5544-71e1-4c78-b8aa-42b2fca50af3",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/login",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Loads the login page once so Laravel's VerifyCsrfToken middleware sets the XSRF-TOKEN cookie in Postman's cookie jar. Run this once before logging in."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Login",
          "id": "bb766f60-2946-4e1a-b68d-c61b597f8dc9",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                {
                  "key": "email",
                  "value": "{{email}}",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "password",
                  "value": "{{password}}",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/login",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Logs in via Breeze's default session-based login. The X-XSRF-TOKEN header is attached automatically by the collection's pre-request script, using the cookie captured in step 1."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
